# Reverse engineering scratchpads. These attach to a running game and dump its
# memory, which makes them development instruments rather than part of the
# payload: useful while working out an offset, worthless to anyone building it.
internal/tools/*.py
internal/tools/inject_on_launch.ps1

# The developer half: crash log, exception recorder, frame profiler. Not part of
# what a user runs, and not published. The build is arranged so this can be
# absent: the headers carry inline no-ops, so the user variant compiles and links
# with the directory missing entirely. Configuring with -DSHADOW_DEV=ON without
# it fails with a message saying so rather than a wall of linker errors.
internal/src/Dev/
